{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-101622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1,{x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-101622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-6x+x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-5x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-101622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-101622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-101622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-5x-3"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-10x-6"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-2x+6"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-5x-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-101622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+10x"] ["math" "-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x"] ["math" "-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+5x"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-3,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-3$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-(-3))(x-(-3))(x-1) \\\\  & =5(x+3)(x+3)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+3)(x+3)(x-1) & =5({x}^{2}+6x+9)(x-1) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+6{x}^{2}-6x+9x-9) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+3x-9) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-104471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+25x-45"] ["math" "5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+5x-25"] ["math" "5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45"] ["math" "5{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+5x-25"] ["math" "5{x}^{3}-25{x}^{2}-15x+45"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic equation has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-3))(x-0)(x-5) \\\\  & =2x(x+3)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x(x+3)(x-5) & =2x({x}^{2}-2x-15) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-15x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-107540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+15x"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+60x"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-30"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-4x-15"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-30x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=0,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-5(x-0)(x-(-4))(x-7) \\\\  & =-5\\,x\\,(x+4)(x-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\,x\\,(x+4)(x-7) & =-5\\,x\\,({x}^{2}-3x-28) \\\\  & =-5({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-28x) \\\\  & =-5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+140x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+140x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-316630" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "140"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104489" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-2,{x}_{2,3}=3\\pm \\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $f(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104489" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=3\\pm \\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-1(x-(-2))(x-(3+\\text{i}))(x-(3-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-(x+2)(x-(3+\\text{i}))(x-(3-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+2)(x-(3+\\text{i}))(x-(3-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -(x+2)({x}^{2}-x(3-\\text{i})-x(3+\\text{i})+(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -(x+2)({x}^{2}-6x+10) & = \\\\ -({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+10x+2{x}^{2}-12x+20) & = \\\\ -{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x-20 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+2x-20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-104489" "fi