 cubic term is $2.$ Find $f(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-1))(x-4\\text{i})(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2(x+1)({x}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 2(x+1)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+16) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-107541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+32"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+32x-32"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+16"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-16"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-107541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/210d2120771bef60b0db703a04a06df395225a0c9a884faf012d55f0ed1f60d6.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-1)(x-(3+2\\text{i}))(x-(3-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)(x-(3+2\\text{i}))(x-(3-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)({x}^{2}-x(3-2\\text{i})-x(3+2\\text{i})+(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)({x}^{2}-6x+13) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+13x-{x}^{2}+6x-13) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}+95x-65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}+95x-65.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-275172" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-27517