nd ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+9x-4{x}^{2}-36 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-12"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+16"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x-14"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8179149af5d820ed0eb2e19e792a4ec4c728c3b52402a63736f26e093952932"} {"question" "e-8799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-8799.json" "file_sha256" "70b15881bf1aa998c0bac3a555d682ce9717d820d670dd3035bc8d3bbf398a9d"} {"question" "e-8799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-8799.json" "file_sha256" "70b15881bf1aa998c0bac3a555d682ce9717d820d670dd3035bc8d3bbf398a9d"} {"question" "e-5792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-5792.json" "file_sha256" "5caa8000ca20e69592f4ec682ca70cc0161c31eb71645f942c86601ea43c591c"} {"question" "e-5792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-5792.json" "file_sha256" "5caa8000ca20e69592f4ec682ca70cc0161c31eb71645f942c86601ea43c591c"}] "usage" {"e-5792" [] "q-101622" [] "q-104469" [] "e-8799" []} "basis" 830 "retractions" [[17592186087906 :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_{1} = x_{2} =-1, x_{3} = 3$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2$. Find $P(x)$."] [17592186087915 :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_{1} =-5$, $x_{2} = 0$, and $x_{3} = 1$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2$. Find $P(x)$."] [17592186087586 :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3$. Find $P(x)$."] [17592186087586 :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_3=1}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the cubic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=3}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3}) &= 3(x - 2)(x - 2)(x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(x - 2)(x - 2)(x - 1) &= 3(x^{2} - 4x + 4)(x - 1) \\\\\n&= 3(x^{3} - x^{2} - 4x^{2} + 4x + 4x - 4) \\\\\n&= 3(x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 8x - 4) \\\\\n&= 3x^{3} - 15x^{2} + 24x - 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12\n$$"] [17592186087511 :question/problem "The Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/896/Source/Images/19c7ba3bb7e7f5410bb6fd0adf39ce0e.png)"] [17592186087511 :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1= 2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= a(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3}) \\\\\n&= (x - 2)(x - (-2 + \\textrm{i}))(x - (-2 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 2)(x - (-2 + \\textrm{i}))(x - (-2 - \\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x - 2)(x^{2} - x(-2 - \\textrm{i}) - x(-2 + \\textrm{i}) + (-2 + \\textrm{i})(-2 - \\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x - 2)(x^{2} + 4x + 5) &=  \\\\\nx^{3} + 4x^{2} + 5x - 2x^{2} - 8x - 10 &=  \\\\\n&= x^{3} + 2x^{2} - 3x - 10 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186084448 17592186084449 17592186084450 17592186084451 17592186084452 17592186084502 17592186084503 17592186084504 17592186084505 17592186084506] "immutable_fields" [[17592186084447 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084447 :answer-field/id] [17592186084447 :answer-field/key] [17592186084447 :answer-field/type] [17592186084501 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084501 :answer-field/id] [17592186084501 :answer-field/key] [17592186084501 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
